1️⃣ Accessors (Formatted / Derived Values)

Accessors allow you to format or calculate values automatically when retrieving data.

📌 Example: Format Price Automatically
app/Models/Property.php
<?php

namespace App\Models;

use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Casts\Attribute;

class Property extends Model
{
    protected $fillable = [
        'title',
        'category_id',
        'agent_id',
        'price',
        'description',
        'address',
        'city',
        'status',
        'image',
    ];

    /*
    |--------------------------------------------------------------------------
    | Accessors
    |--------------------------------------------------------------------------
    */

    // 1️⃣ Format price as currency
    protected function formattedPrice(): Attribute
    {
        return Attribute::make(
            get: fn () => '₹ ' . number_format($this->price, 2)
        );
    }

    // 2️⃣ Capitalize title automatically
    protected function title(): Attribute
    {
        return Attribute::make(
            get: fn ($value) => ucfirst($value)
        );
    }

    // 3️⃣ Full address accessor
    protected function fullAddress(): Attribute
    {
        return Attribute::make(
            get: fn () => $this->address . ', ' . $this->city
        );
    }

    // 4️⃣ Image full URL accessor
    protected function imageUrl(): Attribute
    {
        return Attribute::make(
            get: fn () => $this->image
                ? asset('storage/' . $this->image)
                : asset('images/no-image.png')
        );
    }
}
✅ How to Use in Blade
{{ $property->formatted_price }}
{{ $property->full_address }}
<img src="{{ $property->image_url }}">

No formatting needed in controller anymore ✅

✅ 2️⃣ Mutators (Modify Data Before Saving)

Mutators automatically modify data before saving into database.

📌 Example: Always Store Title in Lowercase
protected function title(): Attribute
{
    return Attribute::make(
        set: fn ($value) => strtolower($value)
    );
}

Now:

Property::create(['title' => 'LUXURY VILLA']);

Database will store:

luxury villa

But accessor will show:

Luxury villa

Very clean system 👍

📌 Example: Auto-trim address
protected function address(): Attribute
{
    return Attribute::make(
        set: fn ($value) => trim($value)
    );
}
✅ 3️⃣ Query Scopes (Reusable Query Logic)

Scopes allow reusable query filters.

📌 Local Scope Example

Add inside Property model:

/*
|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Query Scopes
|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/

// Only active properties
public function scopeActive($query)
{
    return $query->where('status', 'active');
}

// Filter by city
public function scopeCity($query, $city)
{
    return $query->where('city', $city);
}

// Filter by price range
public function scopePriceBetween($query, $min, $max)
{
    return $query->whereBetween('price', [$min, $max]);
}

// Belongs to agent
public function scopeOwnedBy($query, $agentId)
{
    return $query->where('agent_id', $agentId);
}
✅ How to Use Scopes
Example 1: Show only active properties
Property::active()->get();
Example 2: Filter by city
Property::active()->city('Ahmedabad')->get();
Example 3: Price range filter
Property::active()
    ->priceBetween(1000000, 5000000)
    ->get();
Example 4: Agent dashboard
Property::ownedBy(Auth::id())->get();

Controller becomes very clean:

$properties = Property::active()->latest()->paginate(10);
✅ 4️⃣ Advanced Example (Search Scope)
public function scopeSearch($query, $term)
{
    return $query->where(function ($q) use ($term) {
        $q->where('title', 'like', "%$term%")
          ->orWhere('city', 'like', "%$term%");
    });
}

Use:

Property::active()
    ->search($request->search)
    ->paginate(10);
✅ 5️⃣ Combine Everything (Professional Example)
$properties = Property::active()
    ->when($request->city, fn($q) => $q->city($request->city))
    ->when($request->min && $request->max,
        fn($q) => $q->priceBetween($request->min, $request->max))
    ->search($request->search)
    ->latest()
    ->paginate(12);
